A1. A great educator. ~ ENCYCLOPEDIA
A12. This will probably open in the spring. ~ FLOWER
A13. In Kentucky they always curry these before the derby season. ~ FAVORS
A14. A tough deal for the fellow who was hungry. ~ GRISTLE
A15. A Scotch tip. ~ THANKS
A16. The island the con men come from. ~ CRETE
A17. This might be the key to Sing Sing. ~ LA
A18. A teaspoonful after each meal. ~ DOSE
A19. This is what he called his sweetie because she always went up in the air. ~ ROSE
A20. Mix. ~ TOM
A21. This was Greek indeed to Cupid. ~ EROS
A22. The kind of pile a ton of coal makes. ~ ASH
A23. The boss of the barn yard. ~ COW
A24. The manuscript as it was printed. ~ MS
A25. Famous last words. ~ PS
A26. With more sang-froid. ~ SANER
A28. What it is now that women are letting their hair and skirts grow longer. ~ SHAME
A32. "This is so sudden." ~ IMMEDIATELY
A35. Closeups of dress models. ~ SNAPS
A36. This is what he called her because she was all set for a ring. ~ PEARL
A37. Now that this one has become a general, we wonder what pa is going to do. ~ MA
A38. This puts up a red front and does a Rushin' business. (Pardon the omission of &.) ~ AP
A39. What is going on in Spain. ~ RIO
A40. A falsehood. ~ WIG
A41. If this were made better it would not be so good as it is now. ~ BEST
A44. A day of repentance. ~ MON
A45. "The lowing herd." ~ KINE
A46. Orders of the magistrate, among the ancient Romans. ~ ACTA
A47. The kind of a looker that a kibitzer is. ~ ON
A48. What she did for Art's sake. ~ POSED
A49. A man who gets into a thing like this hasn't much sense left. ~ STUPOR
A52. If this seems hard it could be skipped. ~ CAPERED
A54. A beautiful white skin that many women envy. ~ ERMINE
A55. Do not mistake this one for a doorman. ~ HUSSAR
A56. An important thing that goes with a ear which few people discover until they have driven for some time. ~ DEPRECIATION

D1. The swanky few. ~ ELITE
D2. There are many kinds of smells in a restaurant but this one smells the most. ~ NOSE
D3. Reducing hasn't made this weigh less. (abbr.) ~ CWT
D4. When old Father Time turned the pages this was the effect. ~ YELLOWED
D5. Beauty experts tell us this is vanishing and we are glad to hear it. ~ CREAM
D6. Poets explain this frequently. ~ OFT
D7. "I'se regusted." ~ PAH
D8. What the world is trying to do to its debts. ~ EVADE
D9. This one is all forgiving. ~ DONOR
D10. Even this kind of a job is beginning to look attractive. ~ IRKSOME
D11. The first thing they do to new club members. ~ ASSESS
D12. Some are toasted, some are cooled and some are this. ~ FRESH
D14. The number of cold packs it takes for a bridge tournament. ~ GROSS
D16. This is a shaky business. ~ CRAPS
D20. This has its ups and downs but on the whole it is considered a sound business. (plur.). ~ TONES
D23. When the soldiers break this they are allowed no quarter. ~ CAMP
D26. A wee bit of Scotch. ~ SMA
D27. It took a long time for this one to sleep it off. ~ RIP
D28. You may have a hard time getting this one out. ~ STAIN
D29. The man who has faithfully served his country during an era of depression in the face of much opposition. ~ HERO
D30. The number that can ride in a Ford sedan. ~ ALL
D31. This implies self-control. ~ MY
D32. The side one's heart is on. ~ IN
D33. The up and coming man. ~ AERONAUT
D34. What bell-hops have done for a following. ~ PAGED
D35. A delusion and a snare. ~ SPECTRE
D37. What they did to bring gold into the country. ~ MINED
D38. This one has been disgraced and humiliated. ~ ABASED
D40. The way the depression is going to leave the world. ~ WISER
D42. What the cherry tree episode is based upon. ~ STUMP
D43. This ungulates from South America. ~ TAPIR
D44. Where were Chase and San born? ~ MOCHA
D45. The moslems seem to put a lot of faith in this. ~ KORAN
D48. If money talks this speaks Spanish. ~ PESO
D50. The end of 1931 and the beginning of 1932. ~ ONE
D51. This is all the receipt that is necessary to fill this properly. ~ REC
D53. This ends your Greek lesson for today. (Do I hear a sigh?) ~ PSI


